cat <<'EOF' > FIX_SUMMARY.md
# Fix for ExtractCircle Function

## Issue Description
The `ExtractCircle` function in `geo/parse.go` had incorrect logic that caused it to return `true` even when the input map didn't contain valid circle data. Specifically:

1. The function would return `true` even when neither "radius" nor "coordinates" were present in the input map
2. The function would return `true` when only one of "radius" or "coordinates" was present
3. This led to the creation of incomplete GeoShape objects

## Root Cause
The original function had this structure:
```go
func ExtractCircle(thing interface{}) (*geojson.GeoShape, bool) {
    // Initialize rv regardless of input validity

    if thingVal.Kind() == reflect.Map {
        // Process map entries but don't track if required fields were found
        for iter.Next() {
            if iter.Key().String() == "radius" {
                // Set radius but don't track that it was found
            }

            if iter.Key().String() == "coordinates" {
                // Process coordinates but don't track that they were found
            }
        }
    }

    // ALWAYS return true, regardless of whether required data was found
    return rv, true
}
```

## Fix Applied
Modified the function to:
1. Track whether both "radius" and "coordinates" are found using boolean flags
2. Only return `true` if both required fields are present and valid
3. Continue to return `false` immediately if coordinates are found but invalid (existing behavior)

```go
func ExtractCircle(thing interface{}) (*geojson.GeoShape, bool) {
    // ... initialization code ...

    var radiusFound, coordinatesFound bool

    if thingVal.Kind() == reflect.Map {
        for iter.Next() {
            if iter.Key().String() == "radius" {
                rv.Radius = iter.Value().Interface().(string)
                radiusFound = true
                continue
            }

            if iter.Key().String() == "coordinates" {
                lng, lat, found := ExtractGeoPoint(iter.Value().Interface())
                if !found {
                    return nil, false  // Invalid coordinates
                }
                rv.Center = append(rv.Center, lng, lat)
                coordinatesFound = true
            }
        }
    }

    // Only return true if BOTH required fields were found
    return rv, radiusFound && coordinatesFound
}
```

## Impact
This fix ensures that:
1. Circles are only extracted when both radius and coordinates are present
2. Incomplete circle data is properly rejected
3. Downstream processing won't encounter partially initialized GeoShape objects
4. The function behavior is consistent with its documented purpose
EOF
```

